* Stop as a breakpoint. JOSS stops when it reaches the step and hands the
* typewriter back. The user can look at values, change them, and say Go.
1.1 Set t = t + n*2.
1.2 Stop if n = 3.
1.3 Type n, t in form 1.
Form 1:
n = __   sum of squares = ____

Set t = 0.
Do part 1 for n = 1(1)5.
n =  1   sum of squares =    1
n =  2   sum of squares =    5
Stopped by step 1.2.
Type n, t.
       n =       3
       t =      14
Delete step 1.2.
Go.
n =  3   sum of squares =   14
n =  4   sum of squares =   30
n =  5   sum of squares =   55
